<title>AUSTRALIA: Westpac tops turnover with large parcel.</title>
<headline>Westpac tops turnover with large parcel.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westpac Banking Corp topped the turnover lists on Wednesday with one large parcel that went through the market just after midday.</p>
<p>Traders said that brokers County Natwest crossed 15 million Westpac shares at A$7.00, valuing the trade at A$105 million.</p>
<p>But they could not say who was behind the trade.</p>
<p>At 1.30 p.m. (0330 GMT), Westpac shares were seven cents lower at A$7.04.</p>
<p>-- Kevin Morrison 61-2 9373-1813</p>
</text>
